.\" Document native $HEX[] handling and the corrected CR behaviour. New $HEX[] ENCODING section: the decode happens first so the @ scan, -d match, normalization, dedup key and length key all see the real bytes; the wrapper is ASCII with no literal @, so a wrapped address measured as written has no domain and buckets at the width of the wrapper. Records that the decoder matches rehex -u exactly, that a wrapped address therefore dedups against its raw twin, and that output preserves the representation while changing only the content, with the NUL-or-newline override stated as a safety rule rather than a style choice. The CR paragraph is inverted: a trailing CR is now stripped, matching rehex -u and rling, rather than preserved. groff and mandoc both clean.
